{"causes": ["The Norse expansion during the Viking Age fostered a culture of exploration and settlement beyond Scandinavia.", "Accounts of new lands to the west, possibly sighted by earlier voyagers like Naddoddr and Garðar Svavarsson, spurred further investigation.", "Socio-political pressures and land scarcity in Norway motivated individuals to seek new opportunities and territories."], "effects": ["Hrafna-Flóki's voyage provided the first intentional and documented exploration of Iceland by a Norseman.", "His naming of the island as "Ísland" became its enduring designation, shaping its identity.", "Flóki's reports, though mixed, contributed vital geographical intelligence that facilitated later permanent Norse settlement in Iceland."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "naddoddr", "sourceName": "Naddoddr", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "hrafna-flki-vilgerarson", "targetName": "Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson", "context": "Naddoddr's accidental discovery of "Snæland" (Iceland) in the early 9th century likely inspired later intentional voyages, including Flóki's expedition."}, {"sourceSlug": "hrafna-flki-vilgerarson", "sourceName": "Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "name-iceland", "targetName": "Name: Iceland", "context": "Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson is credited with bestowing the enduring name "Ísland" (Iceland) upon the island after observing a fjord full of drift ice during his winter stay."}, {"sourceSlug": "hrafna-flki-vilgerarson", "sourceName": "Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "iceland", "targetName": "Iceland", "context": "Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson's exploration and attempted settlement primarily occurred in the western fjords of Iceland during the late 9th century."}, {"sourceSlug": "landnamabok", "sourceName": "Landnámabók", "verb": "CANONIZES", "targetSlug": "hrafna-flki-vilgerarson", "targetName": "Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson", "context": "The medieval Icelandic manuscript *Landnámabók* serves as the primary historical source documenting Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson's voyage and his role in naming Iceland."}, {"sourceSlug": "hrafna-flki-vilgerarson", "sourceName": "Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "ingolfr-arnarson", "targetName": "Ingólfr Arnarson", "context": "Hrafna-Flóki's exploration and reports on Iceland, despite his personal misfortunes, contributed to the body of knowledge that guided Ingólfr Arnarson's successful permanent settlement of the island around 874 CE."}], "places": [{"name": "Vestfirðir, Iceland", "role": "Landing Site"}, {"name": "Norway", "role": "Origin/Departure Point"}, {"name": "Faroe Islands", "role": "Intermediate Stop"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "hrafna-flóki-vilgerðarson"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q737030", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hrafna-Fl%C3%B3ki_Vilger%C3%B0arson"], "tags": ["Iceland", "Explorers & Navigators", "Europe", "cultural-diffusion", "environmental-history", "geopolitical-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson is remembered as a landmark person of the Medieval era, referenced in 0 Wikipedia language editions. Key lasting impacts include: Expanded geographic knowledge and cultural exchange; Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Hrafna-Flóki's intentional voyage to Iceland and his naming of the island were pivotal steps in the Norse colonization of the North Atlantic. His reconnaissance provided crucial geographical information that directly informed and enabled the subsequent permanent settlement of Iceland, shaping the island's unique historical trajectory.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T07:02:13Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#36223654519", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarsson was a Norseman who intentionally sailed to Iceland. His story is documented in the Landnámabók manuscript; however, the precise year of his arrival is not clear. He was of Norwegian origin.", "newValue": "Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson, a Norwegian Norseman born around 900 CE, holds a foundational place in the saga of Iceland's discovery, renowned as the first Norse explorer to intentionally sail to the island, subsequently naming it "Ísland" (Iceland). His voyage, chronicled in the medieval Icelandic manuscript *Landnámabók*, exemplifies the ambitious spirit of Viking Age exploration and the methodical, albeit sometimes flawed, approach to new land discoveries. Flóki's journey, likely occurring in the late 9th century, predates the permanent settlement by Ingólfr Arnarson, establishing him as a crucial precursor in the Norse expansion across the North Atlantic.

Flóki embarked from Norway, guided by three ravens (hence his epithet, "Hrafna-Flóki," or Raven-Flóki), a distinctive navigational technique for the era. After initial landings in the Faroe Islands, he reached the western fjords of Iceland, specifically Vatnsfjörður in Arnarfjörður. He and his companions spent a winter there, but their lack of preparation, particularly their failure to store fodder for their livestock, led to the demise of their animals. This hardship, combined with the sight of a fjord filled with drift ice, prompted Flóki to bestow the name "Ísland" upon the land, a name that has endured for over a millennium.

While Flóki's attempt at settlement proved unsuccessful, leading to his return to Norway with a mixed report of the new land, his reconnaissance was invaluable. His journey confirmed the existence of a large, habitable island to the west, disseminating crucial geographical knowledge within Norse society. This information, regardless of Flóki's personal misfortunes, directly informed subsequent expeditions and paved the way for the later, successful colonization efforts that established the Icelandic Commonwealth. His story thus serves as a vital chapter in the broader narrative of Norse seafaring and settlement, contributing to Iceland's unique cultural and historical identity."}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-26T07:02:13Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#36223654519", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Educated at in the 500 – 1500 CE", "type": "Person", "year": "500"}, {"title": "Influenced by in the 500 – 1500 CE", "type": "Person", "year": "500"}, {"title": "Born into in the 500 – 1500 CE", "type": "Person", "year": "500"}], "newValue": ["The Norse expansion during the Viking Age fostered a culture of exploration and settlement beyond Scandinavia.", "Accounts of new lands to the west, possibly sighted by earlier voyagers like Naddoddr and Garðar Svavarsson, spurred further investigation.", "Socio-political pressures and land scarcity in Norway motivated individuals to seek new opportunities and territories."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-26T07:02:13Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#36223654519", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Founded through Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson's historical significance", "type": "Person"}, {"title": "Wrote through Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson's historical significance", "type": "Person"}, {"title": "Established through Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson's historical significance", "type": "Person"}, {"title": "Transformed through Hrafna-Flóki Vilgerðarson's historical significance", "type": "Person"}